  "body": "The [interface `EventTarget`](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-eventtarget) specifes the `options` argument to its `addEventListener` method as `optional (AddEventListenerOptions or boolean) options` , which I take as meaning the argument may be omitted.\r\n\r\nHowever, the [actual procedure for how `addEventListener` shall behave](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-eventtarget-addeventlistener), further down the same document, does not appear to specify how to treat the case of omitted `options` argument.\r\n\r\nIs this by design -- implementations are free to behave in a manner they find suitable with regard to omitting the argument, or is this an oversight in the publication?",
